249			<h1>Welcome</h1>
250		</header>
251		<main id="main" tabindex="-1">
252			<section>
253				<p>This is a well-structured, accessible HTML5 document demonstrating modern best practices for semantic markup and inclusive design.</p>
254				<p>
255					It uses semantic landmarks, a skip link for keyboard navigation,
256					and CSS that adapts to your light or dark mode preference.
257				</p>
258				<p>
259					Text and link colors meet WCAG AA contrast in both themes, type scales
260					with your browser's font size, and motion respects your system settings.
261				</p>
262			</section>
263	
264			<section aria-labelledby="features">
265				<h2 id="features">Features</h2>
266				<ul>
267					<li>Semantic HTML structure with proper landmarks</li>
268					<li>Keyboard accessible navigation and focus management</li>
269					<li>Dark mode support with custom color schemes</li>
270					<li>Responsive typography using modern CSS</li>
271					<li>Print-friendly styles for better readability</li>
272					<li>WCAG AA contrast compliance in all color modes</li>
273				</ul>
274			</section>
275	
276			<section aria-labelledby="examples">
277				<h2 id="examples">Examples</h2>
278				<article class="card">
279					<h3>Component Cards</h3>
280					<p>Card components are useful for organizing related content. They include a subtle border and padding for visual separation.</p>
281					<button type="button">Learn More</button>
282				</article>
283	
284				<article class="card">
285					<h3>Interactive Elements</h3>
286					<p>Buttons and links are fully accessible with clear focus states. The button above demonstrates smooth transitions and proper visual feedback.</p>
287					<p>Try using the Tab key to navigate through all interactive elements.</p>
288				</article>
289			</section>
290	
291			<section aria-labelledby="resources">
292				<h2 id="resources">Resources</h2>
293				<p>Want to learn more about web accessibility and semantic HTML? Check out these resources:</p>
294				<ul>
295					<li><a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG21/quickref/">WCAG 2.1 Quick Reference</a></li>
296					<li><a href="https://html.spec.whatwg.org/">HTML Living Standard</a></li>
297					<li><a href="https://www.a11y-101.com/">A11y 101</a></li>
298				</ul>
299			</section>
300		</main>
